# Volatile session files — regenerated each session
.tool-counter
.prev-token-reading
session.yaml
focus.yaml
# T-222: pattern was `tier0-approval` (no leading dot) — never matched the real
# `.tier0-approval` token, so transient Tier-0 grants leaked into commits. Glob the
# `.pending`/`.consumed` siblings too.
.tier0-approval*
# T-410: the Watchtower session signing key — the value that signs fw_session_<port>
# and the CSRF token inside it. It is regenerated on demand by _resolve_secret_key()
# (web/app.py), so it is volatile in exactly the sense this file is for; it was never
# listed, and 371 tracked files under .context/working/ meant it was swept in without
# anyone choosing it. Second instance of the T-222 shape directly above: an ignore file
# that is trusted to cover a directory while the one entry that matters is absent.
.fw-secret-key
